{"id":"mahabharata-7-008","work":"mahabharata","part":7,"partName":"द्रोणपर्व","partNameEn":"Drona Parva","unit":8,"title":"अष्टमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 8 · Dhritarashtra asks about Drona's death","summary":{"en":"Dhritarashtra, hearing that Drona has fallen, asks how the Pandavas and Srinjayas slew him, and what happened to his chariot, bow and skill. Overcome with grief, he asks Sanjaya to pause.","kn":"ದ್ರೋಣ ಬಿದ್ದನೆಂದು ಕೇಳಿ ಧೃತರಾಷ್ಟ್ರ ಪಾಂಡವರು, ಸೃಂಜಯರು ಅವನನ್ನು ಹೇಗೆ ಕೊಂದರೆಂದೂ ಅವನ ರಥ, ಬಿಲ್ಲು, ಕೌಶಲ್ಯಕ್ಕೆ ಏನಾಯಿತೆಂದೂ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ದುಃಖದಿಂದ ಮುಳುಗಿ ಸಂಜಯನಿಗೆ ನಿಲ್ಲಿಸಲು ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"द्रोण के गिरने की बात सुनकर धृतराष्ट्र पूछते हैं कि पाण्डवों और सृंजयों ने उन्हें कैसे मारा, और उनके रथ, धनुष और कौशल का क्या हुआ। शोक से व्याकुल होकर वे संजय से रुकने को कहते हैं।","te":"ద్రోణుడు పడిపోయాడని విని ధృతరాష్ట్రుడు పాండవులు, సృంజయులు అతన్ని ఎలా చంపారని, అతని రథం, విల్లు, నైపుణ్యానికి ఏమైందని అడుగుతాడు. దుఃఖంతో సంజయుని ఆగమంటాడు.","ta":"த்ரோணர் வீழ்ந்ததைக் கேட்ட த்ருதராஷ்டிரன் பாண்டவரும் சிருஞ்சயரும் அவரை எப்படிக் கொன்றனர், அவர் தேர், வில், திறமைக்கு என்ன ஆனது என்று கேட்கிறான். துயரத்தால் மூழ்கி சஞ்சயனை நிறுத்தச் சொல்கிறான்.","ml":"ദ്രോണർ വീണെന്ന് കേട്ട ധൃതരാഷ്ട്രർ, പാണ്ഡവരും സൃഞ്ജയരും അദ്ദേഹത്തെ എങ്ങനെ വധിച്ചു, അദ്ദേഹത്തിന്റെ രഥവും വില്ലും വൈദഗ്ധ്യവും എന്തായി എന്ന് ചോദിക്കുന്നു. ദുഃഖം അടക്കാനാകാതെ അദ്ദേഹം സഞ്ജയനോട് നിർത്താൻ ആവശ്യപ്പെടുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 7.8; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Sep 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"द्रोणाभिषेकपर्व","titleEn":"Dronabhisheka Parva (Drona's consecration)","verses":[{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"किं कुर्वाणं रणे द्रोणं जघ्नुः पाण्डवसृञ्जयाः ।\nतथा निपुणमस्त्रेषु सर्वशस्त्रभृतामपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"What was Drona doing in battle when the Pandavas and Srinjayas killed him, so skilled in weapons, even among all weapon-bearers?"}},{"n":2,"text":"रथभङ्गो बभूवास्य धनुर्वाशीर्यतास्यतः ।\nप्रमत्तो वाभवद्द्रोणस्ततो मृत्युमुपेयिवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Was his chariot broken, or his bow shattered as he shot, or was Drona careless, and so met his death?"}},{"n":3,"text":"कथं नु पार्षतस्तात शत्रुभिर्दुष्प्रधर्षणम् ।\nकिरन्तमिषुसंघातान्रुक्मपुङ्खाननेकशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"How, my dear, could Prishata's son kill a man hard for enemies to assault, who scattered volleys of gold-feathered arrows many times over,"}},{"n":4,"text":"क्षिप्रहस्तं द्विजश्रेष्ठं कृतिनं चित्रयोधिनम् ।\nदूरेषुपातिनं दान्तमस्त्रयुद्धे च पारगम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"that best of brahmins of quick hands, accomplished, a varied fighter, shooting far, self-controlled and master of weapon-fighting?"}},{"n":5,"text":"पाञ्चालपुत्रो न्यवधीद्दिष्ट्या स वरमच्युतम् ।\nकुर्वाणं दारुणं कर्म रणे यत्तं महारथम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"By luck the Panchala prince slew that unfailing best of men, a great chariot-warrior doing fierce deeds in battle, ever intent."}},{"n":6,"text":"व्यक्तं दिष्टं हि बलवत्पौरुषादिति मे मतिः ।\nयद्द्रोणो निहतः शूरः पार्षतेन महात्मना ॥","meaning":{"en":"It seems to me plain that fate is stronger than manly effort, since brave Drona was killed by the great-souled son of Prishata."}},{"n":7,"text":"अस्त्रं चतुर्विधं वीरे यस्मिन्नासीत्प्रतिष्ठितम् ।\nतमिष्वस्त्रवराचार्यं द्रोणं शंससि मे हतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"You tell me that Drona is slain, the best teacher of the bow and weapons, in whom the fourfold weapon-knowledge was established in a hero."}},{"n":8,"text":"श्रुत्वा हतं रुक्मरथं वैयाघ्रपरिवारणम् ।\nजातरूपपरिष्कारं नाद्य शोकमपानुदे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing that the man of the golden chariot, with his tiger-skin cover and gold fittings, is dead, I cannot cast off my grief today."}},{"n":9,"text":"न नूनं परदुःखेन कश्चिन्म्रियति संजय ।\nयत्र द्रोणमहं श्रुत्वा हतं जीवामि न म्रिये ॥","meaning":{"en":"Surely no one dies of another's sorrow, Sanjaya, since I, hearing that Drona is slain, go on living and do not die."}},{"n":10,"text":"अश्मसारमयं नूनं हृदयं सुदृढं मम ।\nयच्छ्रुत्वा निहतं द्रोणं शतधा न विदीर्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"My heart must be made of steel, firm and strong, since it does not split into a hundred pieces on hearing Drona is dead."}},{"n":11,"text":"ब्राह्मे वेदे तथेष्वस्त्रे यमुपासन्गुणार्थिनः ।\nब्राह्मणा राजपुत्राश्च स कथं मृत्युना हतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"How was he killed by death, he whom brahmins and princes, seeking excellence, served for the Vedic lore and the science of the bow?"}},{"n":12,"text":"शोषणं सागरस्येव मेरोरिव विसर्पणम् ।\nपतनं भास्करस्येव न मृष्ये द्रोणपातनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I cannot bear the fall of Drona any more than the drying of the ocean, the shifting of Meru, or the falling of the sun."}},{"n":13,"text":"दृप्तानां प्रतिषेद्धासीद्धार्मिकानां च रक्षिता ।\nयोऽत्याक्षीत्कृपणस्यार्थे प्राणानपि परंतपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He was the restrainer of the proud and the protector of the righteous, who would give up even his life for the sake of a wretched man."}},{"n":14,"text":"मन्दानां मम पुत्राणां जयाशा यस्य विक्रमे ।\nबृहस्पत्युशनस्तुल्यो बुद्ध्या स निहतः कथम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"On his prowess my foolish sons rested their hope of victory. How was he killed, equal to Brihaspati and Ushanas in wisdom?"}},{"n":15,"text":"ते च शोणा बृहन्तोऽश्वाः सैन्धवा हेममालिनः ।\nरथे वातजवा युक्ताः सर्वशब्दातिगा रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"And those big red Sindhu horses with gold garlands, yoked to his chariot, swift as the wind, beyond all sound in battle,"}},{"n":16,"text":"बलिनो घोषिणो दान्ताः सैन्धवाः साधुवाहिनः ।\nदृढाः संग्राममध्येषु कच्चिदासन्न विह्वलाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"strong, loud, tamed, good pullers, steady in the middle of battles, did they ever falter?"}},{"n":17,"text":"करिणां बृंहतां युद्धे शङ्खदुन्दुभिनिस्वनम् ।\nज्याक्षेपशरवर्षाणां शस्त्राणां च सहिष्णवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They endured the roar of trumpeting elephants, the sound of conches and drums, the twang of bowstrings, showers of arrows and weapons in battle."}},{"n":18,"text":"आशंसन्तः पराञ्जेतुं जितश्वासा जितव्यथाः ।\nहयाः प्रजविताः शीघ्रा भारद्वाजरथोद्वहाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those quick horses, hoping to beat the enemy, with their breath and weariness mastered, trained to speed, carried Bharadvaja's chariot."}},{"n":19,"text":"ते स्म रुक्मरथे युक्ता नरवीरसमाहिताः ।\nकथं नाभ्यतरंस्तात पाण्डवानामनीकिनीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yoked to the golden chariot and guided by a hero, how did they not break through the Pandava army, my dear?"}},{"n":20,"text":"जातरूपपरिष्कारमास्थाय रथमुत्तमम् ।\nभारद्वाजः किमकरोच्छूरः संक्रन्दनो युधि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Mounted on his excellent chariot with gold fittings, what did the hero Bharadvaja's son, like Indra roaring in battle, do?"}},{"n":21,"text":"विद्यां यस्योपजीवन्ति सर्वलोकधनुर्भृतः ।\nस सत्यसंधो बलवान्द्रोणः किमकरोद्युधि ॥","meaning":{"en":"What did mighty Drona of true pledge do in the fight, he on whose knowledge all the archers of the world depend?"}},{"n":22,"text":"दिवि शक्रमिव श्रेष्ठं महामात्रं धनुर्भृताम् ।\nके नु तं रौद्रकर्माणं युद्धे प्रत्युद्ययू रथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Which chariot-warriors met in battle that man of terrible deeds, chief among bowmen like Shakra in heaven?"}},{"n":23,"text":"ननु रुक्मरथं दृष्ट्वा प्रद्रवन्ति स्म पाण्डवाः ।\nदिव्यमस्त्रं विकुर्वाणं सेनां क्षिण्वन्तमव्ययम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Did the Pandavas not run when they saw the golden chariot, as he unleashed divine weapons and cut through the army, himself unharmed?"}},{"n":24,"text":"उताहो सर्वसैन्येन धर्मराजः सहानुजः ।\nपाञ्चाल्यप्रग्रहो द्रोणं सर्वतः समवारयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Or did Dharmaraja with all his army and his younger brothers, with the Panchala as his leader, surround Drona on every side?"}},{"n":25,"text":"नूनमावारयत्पार्थो रथिनोऽन्यानजिह्मगैः ।\nततो द्रोणं समारोहत्पार्षतः पापकर्मकृत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Surely Arjuna held back the other chariot-fighters with straight arrows, and then the sinful Prishata's son mounted against Drona."}},{"n":26,"text":"न ह्यन्यं परिपश्यामि वधे कंचन शुष्मिणः ।\nधृष्टद्युम्नादृते रौद्रात्पाल्यमानात्किरीटिना ॥","meaning":{"en":"I see no other, in his killing, who was strong enough, except the terrible Dhrishtadyumna, protected by Arjuna."}},{"n":27,"text":"तैर्वृतः सर्वतः शूरैः पाञ्चाल्यापसदस्ततः ।\nकेकयैश्चेदिकारूषैर्मत्स्यैरन्यैश्च भूमिपैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Surrounded on all sides by those heroes, by the Kekayas, Chedis, Karushas, Matsyas and other kings, that low Panchala,"}},{"n":28,"text":"व्याकुलीकृतमाचार्यं पिपीलैरुरगं यथा ।\nकर्मण्यसुकरे सक्तं जघानेति मतिर्मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"I think, struck down the teacher, who was harassed like a snake by ants and absorbed in a hard task."}},{"n":29,"text":"योऽधीत्य चतुरो वेदान्सर्वानाख्यानपञ्चमान् ।\nब्राह्मणानां प्रतिष्ठासीत्स्रोतसामिव सागरः ।\nस कथं ब्राह्मणो वृद्धः शस्त्रेण वधमाप्तवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who studied all four Vedas with the Akhyanas as the fifth, who was the support of brahmins as the ocean is of rivers, how did that aged brahmin die by a weapon?"}},{"n":30,"text":"अमर्षणो मर्षितवान्क्लिश्यमानः सदा मया ।\nअनर्हमाणः कौन्तेयः कर्मणस्तस्य तत्फलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The son of Kunti, ever intolerant of wrong, bore it while I afflicted him; unworthy of such treatment, he has now reaped the fruit of that deed."}},{"n":31,"text":"यस्य कर्मानुजीवन्ति लोके सर्वधनुर्भृतः ।\nस सत्यसंधः सुकृती श्रीकामैर्निहतः कथम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He on whose action all the archers in the world depended, true to his word and righteous, how was he killed by those who desired wealth?"}},{"n":32,"text":"दिवि शक्र इव श्रेष्ठो महासत्त्वो महाबलः ।\nस कथं निहतः पार्थैः क्षुद्रमत्स्यैर्यथा तिमिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Like Shakra supreme in heaven, great in spirit and great in strength, how was he killed by the Parthas, as a tiny fish is eaten by a timi whale?"}},{"n":33,"text":"क्षिप्रहस्तश्च बलवान्दृढधन्वारिमर्दनः ।\nन यस्य जीविताकाङ्क्षी विषयं प्राप्य जीवति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Quick-handed, strong, a firm bowman who crushed enemies, no one who wished to live and came within his reach lived."}},{"n":34,"text":"यं द्वौ न जहतः शब्दौ जीवमानं कदाचन ।\nब्राह्मश्च वेदकामानां ज्याघोषश्च धनुर्भृताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Two sounds never left him while he lived: the chanting of Veda by those eager for learning, and the twang of bowstrings by archers."}},{"n":35,"text":"नाहं मृष्ये हतं द्रोणं सिंहद्विरदविक्रमम् ।\nकथं संजय दुर्धर्षमनाधृष्ययशोबलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I cannot bear that Drona is slain, with the prowess of a lion or an elephant, how, Sanjaya, one so unassailable in fame and strength?"}},{"n":36,"text":"केऽरक्षन्दक्षिणं चक्रं सव्यं के च महात्मनः ।\nपुरस्तात्के च वीरस्य युध्यमानस्य संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Who guarded the right wheel of the great soul, and who the left, and who fought before the hero as he fought in battle?"}},{"n":37,"text":"के च तत्र तनुं त्यक्त्वा प्रतीपं मृत्युमाव्रजन् ।\nद्रोणस्य समरे वीराः केऽकुर्वन्त परां धृतिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And who there gave up his body and met death facing him, and which heroes showed supreme steadiness in Drona's battle?"}},{"n":38,"text":"एतदार्येण कर्तव्यं कृच्छ्रास्वापत्सु संजय ।\nपराक्रमेद्यथाशक्त्या तच्च तस्मिन्प्रतिष्ठितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"This is what a noble man should do in dire calamities, Sanjaya: strive as far as he can, and that was fully established in him."}},{"n":39,"text":"मुह्यते मे मनस्तात कथा तावन्निवर्त्यताम् ।\nभूयस्तु लब्धसंज्ञस्त्वा परिप्रक्ष्यामि संजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"My mind is confused, my dear. Let the tale be put aside for now. When I have recovered my senses I will ask you more, Sanjaya."}}]}]}